From: uDroid graphics runtime
Subject: [PATCH] libhybris: redirect raw Bionic thread-pointer reads

Android vendor libraries and Bionic libc contain inline MRS TPIDR_EL0 reads
that bypass symbol interposition. In a glibc PRoot process those reads resolve
against the host TCB, so Bionic's errno path can dereference glibc state as a
pthread_internal_t and crash.

Patch AArch64 thread-pointer reads through per-library thunks, redirect them to
the isolated Bionic TCB already maintained in uDroid's static TLS reserve, and
populate TLS_SLOT_THREAD_ID with a per-thread shadow. This keeps both Bionic's
negative TLS slot and errno/thread fields away from glibc's TCB.

Adapted from Nikita Ukhrenkov's libhybris TLS patcher:
https://github.com/wmww/libhybris/commit/77bda7a0e47b4426998c0b13fd2d8dd15c4c0b36

Includes thunk allocation and instruction encoding corrections from Sophie
Winter's follow-up:
https://github.com/wmww/libhybris/commit/56954bf7bc4b0408b29273fbe838b429d600d597

The TLS_SLOT_THREAD_ID shadow follows the implementation and Android 17 crash
analysis in:
https://github.com/wmww/libhybris/commit/a7674b19cbd52600e14c990d3897a692140db2ed
---
